                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0ca057e2-6fcf-3bc2-8b85-87d09c8bc53c",
                        "entry_id": "c7a6b80e-ede2-3a47-b2ef-48af5cf309d9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The still burning or wholly burnt tobacco plug in a pipe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0a161c1-ba63-457a-9f25-9731f67f7c45",
                                "sense_id": "0ca057e2-6fcf-3bc2-8b85-87d09c8bc53c",
                                "text": "1892, Richard Oliver Heslop, Northumberland Words. English Dialect Society - Kegan Paul et al.\nIn refilling a pipe, where twist is smoked, a common practice is to save the dottle and put it on the top of the new-filled pipe. \"Aw like a baccy dottle to leet wiv.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d25e1e2-8f20-47f1-a331-b57e348a084d",
                                "sense_id": "0ca057e2-6fcf-3bc2-8b85-87d09c8bc53c",
                                "text": "one hand guards the burning dottle of my pipe from the force of the wind"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f5007d6a-025a-4c71-8331-160ea961e5a5",
                                "sense_id": "0ca057e2-6fcf-3bc2-8b85-87d09c8bc53c",
                                "text": "I clenched my pipe in my right fist and poked at the dottle busily with various fingers, first one then another, of my left hand."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2294371b-534a-4236-8a67-fb68e27d6ca6",
                                "sense_id": "0ca057e2-6fcf-3bc2-8b85-87d09c8bc53c",
                                "text": "He tapped out the dottle on the deck, locked the steering oar in position, and commenced repacking his pipe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c752fe0b-20ef-42cc-8a49-2cb1d5008e7d",
                                "sense_id": "0ca057e2-6fcf-3bc2-8b85-87d09c8bc53c",
                                "text": "I fiddle and scrape and poke for a while, banging out the dottle from my previous pipeful into an ashtray and puffing down the stem like a horn player warming up his trumpet."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2a1a2b8a-c0b1-390b-a867-79352651de64",
                        "entry_id": "c7a6b80e-ede2-3a47-b2ef-48af5cf309d9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A baby's dummy, pacifier."
                        ],
